# POOBank — Finance CLI

A simple command-line financial application built with Python as a personal learning project.

The main goal of this project is to explore Object-Oriented Programming (OOP) and understand how to apply programming concepts to a real application.

This is my first attempt at building a project independently, so the focus is on learning, practicing and improving along the way.

## Current Features

- [x] Account creation
- [x] Deposit operations
- [x] Withdrawal operations
- [x] Balance consultation

## In Progress

- [ ] JSON data persistence
- [ ] Login and authentication
- [ ] Multiple account support
- [ ] Improved input validation

## Technologies

- Python
- Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)
- JSON

## Project Structure

```text
Finance_CLI/
├── finance/
│   ├── models/
│   │   ├── conta.py
│   │   └── transacao.py
│   └── services/
│       └── persistencia.py
├── main.py
├── .gitignore
└── README.md
```

## Running the Project

Clone the repository:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/DEVkaionasci/Finance_CLI.git
```

Navigate to the project directory:

```bash
cd Finance_CLI
```

Install the required dependencies and run:

```bash
python main.py
```

